  "body": "Empty key in JSON return of the whois endpoint(API).\r\n\r\n`/_matrix/client/r0/admin/whois/{userId}`\r\n\r\nExample return:\r\n\r\n```\r\n   {\r\n  \"user_id\": \"something_name\",\r\n  \"devices\": {\r\n    \"\": {\r\n      \"sessions\": [\r\n        {\r\n          \"connections\": [\r\n            {\r\n              \"ip\": \"225.225.225.225\",\r\n              \"user_agent\": \"something\",\r\n              \"last_seen\": 1504266816737\r\n            }\r\n        }\r\n      ]\r\n    }\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nOne of the json key is an empty string \"\". I can't parse the json properly with that empty \"\" in there. Perhaps it would help if it put \"Unknown\" or something as device name. Anyway, I don't think device name is also working in the main code of Matrix-Synapse since I have multiple devices using RIOT.im and everything is lumped into a single \"\" device. \r\n\r\nIssue reference:\r\nhttps://stackoverflow.com/questions/46985605/how-do-i-call-an-object-property-with-empty-property-name",
